course: dictionary
lesson: 5796
title: Machinery
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Machinery is a noun. It means machines, especially big ones, such as farm machinery. It can also mean the moving parts inside a machine.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «Keep away from machinery» is a safety warning. The words keep away tell you that machines can hurt you, so machinery means machines.
explain: The word can also mean a system that makes something work, like «the machinery of government». Here it is not about metal at all. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Machinery is uncountable, so we say some machinery or heavy machinery, not a machinery or two machineries.
fact: Machinery means machines in general, especially large ones, like farm machinery.
fact: Machinery can also mean the moving parts inside a machine.
fact: «Keep away from machinery» is a warning that machines can be dangerous.
fact: «The machinery of government» means the system that makes government work.
fact: Machinery is uncountable: say heavy machinery, not a machinery.
exercise: «Keep away from the farm machinery.» What does machinery mean here? | *Machines, especially large ones | A hot drink | A soft kind of cloth | Rows of growing plants
exercise: «All living things share the same basic cell machinery.» What does machinery mean here? | Warm, soft blankets | *The moving parts that make cells work | Large trucks in a field | A place where food is sold
exercise: Which phrase uses machinery correctly? | many machinerys | two machineries | *heavy machinery | a machinery
test: «The machinery of government is slow to change.» What does machinery mean here? | Large metal machines in a factory | The moving parts of a bicycle | *The system that makes government work | A wooden toy box
test: Which sentence is a warning about danger? | *«Keep away from the machinery, it can hurt you.» | «We visited the machinery museum on Sunday.» | «The machinery is painted bright green.» | «The machinery was new and shiny.»
exam: What does machinery mean in «Keep children away from machinery on building sites»? | *Machines, especially large ones | Building bricks | Warm, comfortable rooms | The workers who build houses
